Haricots Verts Amandine
Serves: 5
Prep: 10 min
Cook: 15 min
Total: 25 min
Source: Serious Eats, J. Kenji López-Alt
Equipment: Large pot, Bowl of iced water, Spider or tongs, Medium skillet, Kitchen towels

Toss (heat): Add the beans and toss until **hot and glossy**. Season.
  Emulsify (heat, 30 s): Add the lemon juice and **1–2 Tbsp water**. High heat; shake the pan hard until the sauce is **glossy**.
    Toast (heat, ~7 min): Butter and almonds over **medium-low**, stirring, until **deeply browned**, ~5 min. Add garlic and shallot; **2 min** more.
      - 35 g = 3 Tbsp | Unsalted butter
      - 85 g = 3 oz | Slivered almonds
      Slice: Peel and thinly slice.
        - 2 cloves | Garlic
        - 1 | Shallots
    Squeeze: Juice the lemon.
      - 1 | Lemon | for 1½ Tbsp juice
  Blanch (heat, 3 min, then set aside): Trim the stem ends. Into well-salted boiling water until **tender-crisp**, then straight into iced water. Drain and dry well.
    - 450 g = 1 lb | Green beans | haricots verts
    - for the water | Kosher salt
    - plenty | Ice
